# GEMINI_API_KEY: Required for Gemini AI API calls.
# AI Studio automatically injects this at runtime from user secrets.
# Users configure this via the Secrets panel in the AI Studio UI.
GEMINI_API_KEY="MY_GEMINI_API_KEY"

# APP_URL: The URL where this applet is hosted.
# AI Studio automatically injects this at runtime with the Cloud Run service URL.
# Used for self-referential links, OAuth callbacks, and API endpoints.
APP_URL="MY_APP_URL"

# DATABASE_URL: Optional. If set, the server persists to this Postgres database
# instead of the local server_db.json file (see CLAUDE.md "Database Architecture").
# Use the Supabase "Session pooler" connection string, not "Direct connection" -
# the direct-connection host is IPv6-only on the free tier and will fail to
# connect from networks without IPv6 routing. Get it from: Supabase dashboard ->
# your project -> Connect -> Connection string -> Session pooler.
# Format: postgresql://postgres.<project-ref>:<password>@aws-0-<region>.pooler.supabase.com:5432/postgres
DATABASE_URL="postgresql://postgres.MY_PROJECT_REF:MY_PASSWORD@aws-0-MY_REGION.pooler.supabase.com:5432/postgres"

# TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN / TELEGRAM_BOOKING_CHAT_ID: Optional. If both are set, a
# Telegram message is sent to TELEGRAM_BOOKING_CHAT_ID every time a customer
# submits a booking. If either is unset, this feature silently no-ops - a
# booking is never blocked or delayed by it (see server.ts,
# sendTelegramBookingNotification). Create a bot via @BotFather to get a
# token; message the bot (or add it to a group) and call
# https://api.telegram.org/bot<TOKEN>/getUpdates to find the numeric chat_id.
TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN="MY_TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN"
TELEGRAM_BOOKING_CHAT_ID="MY_TELEGRAM_CHAT_ID"

# SUPABASE_URL / SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY: Optional. If both are set, staff can
# upload a product photo directly in the admin product form (Inventaris) instead
# of only pasting an image URL - the browser resizes/converts it to WebP, the
# server uploads it to Supabase Storage, and the resulting public URL is
# auto-filled into the same image field. If either is unset, uploading returns a
# clear "not configured" error and the manual URL field still works as before -
# it never blocks saving a product either way.
# Get SUPABASE_URL from: Supabase dashboard -> your project -> Project Settings
# -> API -> Project URL. Get SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY from the same page's
# `service_role` secret - this key bypasses Row Level Security, so it must only
# ever be used server-side and never sent to the client.
# One-time manual setup required before this works: create a bucket named
# exactly "bilbo-product-images" in the dashboard's Storage section (bucket
# name cannot be changed after creation - must match PRODUCT_IMAGE_BUCKET in
# server.ts exactly, or uploads fail with a 500 once Supabase Storage 404s on
# the mismatched bucket name). On the create-bucket dialog, enable all 3
# toggles: "Public bucket" (needed for the resulting URLs to load directly in
# <img> tags with no auth), "Restrict file size" set to 5 MB, and "Restrict MIME
# types" set to "image/webp" (the browser always converts to WebP before
# uploading, so nothing else should ever need to be accepted). Both restrictions
# are enforced by Supabase's Storage backend itself, not just client-side.
SUPABASE_URL="https://MY_PROJECT_REF.supabase.co"
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY="MY_SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY"
# On the create-bucket dialog's "Restrict MIME types", use "image/webp,image/png"
# (not just image/webp) - Safari's canvas can't encode WebP and silently
# substitutes PNG instead of throwing, so both are legitimate outputs of the
# browser-side conversion, never anything else.

# WUZZPAY_API_KEY / WUZZPAY_MERCHANT_ID / WUZZPAY_ENV: Optional. If the first
# two are set, the real WuzzPay payment gateway is enabled (QRIS / bank VA /
# e-wallet) for customer checkout. If either is unset, the payment routes
# return 503 and the client falls back to the legacy manual QRIS-mock/WhatsApp
# flow untouched (see GET /api/payment-config, server.ts) - this also doubles
# as an instant kill-switch in production if something goes wrong.
# Get WUZZPAY_API_KEY from the WuzzPay Dashboard -> API keys (sandbox and
# production have separate keys - do not mix them). WUZZPAY_ENV controls which
# API host is used: "sandbox" (default if unset - the safe choice) hits
# api-gateway-devel.wuzzpay.com; only set it to "production" once ready to
# take real payments.
WUZZPAY_API_KEY="MY_WUZZPAY_API_KEY"
WUZZPAY_MERCHANT_ID="WZ1600015"
WUZZPAY_ENV="sandbox"

# WUZZPAY_WEBHOOK_SECRET: Optional. Verifies the x-wuzzpay-signature header on
# incoming POST /api/webhooks/wuzzpay calls (hex HMAC-SHA256 of
# "{x-wuzzpay-timestamp}.{raw body}" - confirmed against a real delivery,
# never published in WuzzPay's own docs). Generated once (one-time reveal) in
# the WuzzPay Dashboard -> Webhooks. If unset, signature verification is
# skipped entirely - not a security hole, since the webhook payload is never
# trusted for the actual state change either way (see server.ts's
# verifyAndSettleOrderPayment); this is defense in depth on top of that, not
# the only guard.
WUZZPAY_WEBHOOK_SECRET="MY_WUZZPAY_WEBHOOK_SECRET"
